### [Backplane schematic nearly complete]($section.id('2026-02-16T00:00:00').data('author','xq'))

I've been working in silence on the Backplane schematic for months now.

Now I'm confident it won't change much anymore and I've performed a lot of
[BOM refinement](https://www.designtodevice.com/blog/bom-optimization-strategies) to reduce the
complexity of the board and also decrease the manufacturing price.

To estimate the required PCB space the parts will take, i've roughly layouted 
the connectors and all required parts onto the PCB shape:

> []($block.attrs('pictures','large'))
> []($image.siteAsset('img/devlog/2026/2026-02-16_pcb-is-full.webp').linked(true))

Tight, but most likely doable.

The schematic is also making great progress, with only some minor touchups and
refinements necessary for a first produced version.

Now that this state is reached, I've finally got a fairly reliable estimation for the price of the Backplane materials:

> []($block.attrs('figures','large'))
> [Price at DigiKey for 1]($image.siteAsset('img/devlog/2026/2026-02-16_price-1.webp').linked(true))
> [Price at DigiKey for 100]($image.siteAsset('img/devlog/2026/2026-02-16_price-100.webp').linked(true))

My original estimation was "80€ for 100 PCBs", but it looks like i'm down to "50€ for the parts on the PCBs" which is really really awesome.

The bare PCB would cost 3.13 € per Backplane with 4 layers/ENIG or 3.98 € with 6 layers/ENIG.

Now I need an estimation for the assembly cost, then we'll have reliable numbers for the final Backplane PCB prices.

